                                "sense_id": "60aa08d0-068c-3b40-bf56-8867bb555ad9",
                                "text": "“We can reckon on killing a stag, if he will stand still, at a hundred and fifty yards,” Ned said, “or running, at a hundred; don’t you think so?”\n“Well, six times out of seven we ought to at any rate,” Tom replied, “or our Devonshire archership has deserted us.”"
                            }
